think Read KYRI + RADIANT_STYLE to write in voice, then REMEMBER, the itineraries, the top session logs, and REDS. State of play: live edge is Season G open-media; newest rung image/morphology.rye (dilate/erode) GREEN at nib a4cfcc4518. Standfast clear -- every REDS row closed, released, or resting as custody-gated errata (#75, a deep-debride custody gate). The Microkernel double-seat leads Lindy-first yet its only ungated move is study behind a web-fetch gate, so this lap grows Season G.
think Lindy-first crux-first: the morphology log named the top-hat and the morphological gradient as its siblings. The gradient is the crux -- the DETECT verb of the morphology floor (the outline every region boundary descends from), the exact parallel to how edges is the detect verb of the convolution floor, and the harder-solvable of the two. Grepped image/: no morphology-derived module exists, a clean gap.
think Design the complete rung by sameness-is-the-macro: one subtraction over three operand pairs. The full gradient dilate - erode is a boundary two pixels thick; it decomposes exactly into the outer ring (dilate - src, just outside a shape) plus the inner ring (src - erode, the shape's own edge). Extensivity gives dilate >= src >= erode at every pixel, so both one-sided differences are non-negative -- no byte underflows -- and their sum is the full gradient exactly, a valid byte with no saturation. The additive law is the crux to prove.
think Built image/morphology_gradient.rye leaning only on morphology.rye (dilate/erode) + qoi -- the one new operation is subtract_bytes, asserting high >= low before every write. gradient / gradient_outer / gradient_inner, each guarded up front through morphology's own guard so a refusal allocates nothing. Wrote tools/morphology_gradient_witness.rish in the family idiom (native contains, per REDS #85/#76).
obs Two honest fixes on the way to GREEN. First: the intermediate Pixmaps are read-only here (freed, not mutated), so Zig demanded const not var -- corrected. Second, the real one: the block scene has flat alpha 255 everywhere, so the gradient's alpha channel is uniformly 0 (a flat channel has no transition). A dark gradient pixel is therefore fully-transparent black (0,0,0,0), not opaque black -- the dark-region checks now compare against that blank, which reinforces the documented pure-difference-image semantics rather than papering over it.
obs Version stamp discipline: my first draft future-dated the version const and the REMEMBER git-nib to 110000; corrected both to the real clock 104307 read from TZ=America/New_York (the REDS #75 lesson -- never fabricate a stamp ahead of the clock).
obs Council rota lap read item 13, the happy-zone-and-the-thin-edge foundation. It fits: this rung's whole proof lives in the happy zone -- a fast, isolated, exact selftest with no window, no network, no device; the definition crux (gradient == dilate - erode) is a contract check across the seam to morphology's two verbs, this rung the asker and morphology the answerer.
obs GREEN on the first full metal run after the two fixes: radius 0 the degenerate blank gradient; gradient == dilate - erode byte-for-byte through morphology's own verbs (the definition crux); a boundary lit to 255 in the color channels with both flat regions dark; the additive law holding on a colored translucent field with no saturation; the two rings disjoint and one-sided (outer just outside a shape, inner the shape's own edge); a flat field uniformly blank; alpha measured like any channel; QOI round-trip byte-for-byte; over-max radius and empty source refusing by name; determinism. TAME bans clean, width exit 0, plain 7-bit ASCII, living-docs advisory-GREEN, living-card GREEN.
loom witness=morphology_gradient_witness checks=13 result=green build=first_pass
